# shellcheck shell=sh
# build/cflags -- the hardening every C program we ship is compiled with.
#
# Sourced by build/forge, build/staging and build/aurbridge; one place,
# so the three cannot drift. tools/checksec.sh is the gate that proves
# each flag reached the binary (and, with --selftest, that it fails on
# a binary built without them). Ferry's helpers carry the same line in
# src/ferry/install.sh, which builds inside the image where this file
# is not.
#
# Ubuntu's gcc already defaults to most of these. They are spelled out
# because a default is not a promise: another toolchain, or a later
# Ubuntu, may not -- and -z now (full RELRO) is not a default at all.

# Linux programs (dynamically linked).
HARDEN_CFLAGS="-O2 -D_FORTIFY_SOURCE=3 -fstack-protector-strong \
-fstack-clash-protection -fcf-protection=full -fPIE -pie -Wl,-z,relro,-z,now"

# Linux programs that must be static (PID 1 of the staging environment
# and its screen): the same, position-independent all the same, so even
# PID 1 gets ASLR.
HARDEN_STATIC="-O2 -D_FORTIFY_SOURCE=3 -fstack-protector-strong \
-fstack-clash-protection -fcf-protection=full -fPIE -static-pie -Wl,-z,relro,-z,now"

# The Windows installer (mingw-w64): ASLR with a 64-bit base, DEP, and
# the stack protector (mingw-w64 >= 11 carries its own __stack_chk_fail).
HARDEN_PE="-fstack-protector-strong -Wl,--dynamicbase,--nxcompat,--high-entropy-va"
